  "verdict_rule": "per explanation method, from the deletion test (top 5 features replaced by the background median; the random baseline deletes 5 random features, so it is 5 of N features and N is reported): the share of flows whose drop beats their random drop gets a binomial 95% Wilson interval (n = the flows tested, reported). 'inconclusive' if that interval includes 0.5; otherwise 'faithful' if the mean drop is at least 2x the random drop and the interval lies above 0.5; 'weak' if the interval lies above 0.5 and the ratio is at least 1.5 (but under 2); 'not better than random' if the interval lies below 0.5 or the ratio is under 1; 'inconclusive' otherwise; 'not run' if the method or file is absent. With about 10 flows per class the interval is wide (about +-10 points at 100 flows): a verdict is a summary, not a test"
}